{"name":"Yellow Warbler","hex":"#ffba6f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow warbler","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of certain small, yellow-colored songbird, including:\nA yellow New World warbler (family Parulidae), of genus Setophaga, such as Setophaga petechia.\nA yellow Old World warbler, any of several species of family Acrocephalidae, in genera Iduna and Calamonastides.","A yellow New World warbler (family Parulidae), of genus Setophaga, such as Setophaga petechia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow_warbler"}],"entries":[{"title":"American yellow warbler","blocks":[{"text":"The American yellow warbler, also known as the northern yellow warbler, is a New World warbler. It is a widespread migratory species in the diverse genus Setophaga, that breeds in most parts of North America. It was formerly considered to be conspecific with the non-migratory mangrove warbler."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Yellow_warbler_%2882905%29.jpg/330px-Yellow_warbler_%2882905%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_yellow_warbler"},{"title":"Warbler","blocks":[{"text":"Various Passeriformes are commonly referred to as warblers. They are not necessarily closely related to one another, but share some characteristics, such as being fairly small, vocal, and insectivorous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Flickr_-_Rainbirder_-_Wood_Warbler_%28Phylloscopus_sibilatrix%29.jpg/330px-Flickr_-_Rainbirder_-_Wood_Warbler_%28Phylloscopus_sibilatrix%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warbler"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Dendroica_petechia3_CC1.jpg/500px-Dendroica_petechia3_CC1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Dendroica_petechia3_CC1.jpg/500px-Dendroica_petechia3_CC1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Female yellow warbler attending nestlings, Yukon Flats National Wildlife Refuge, Alaska, United States","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADendroica_petechia3_CC1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Yellow_Warblers_3537092053.jpg/500px-Yellow_Warblers_3537092053.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Yellow_Warblers_3537092053.jpg/1280px-Yellow_Warblers_3537092053.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Yellow_Warblers_3537092053.jpg/500px-Yellow_Warblers_3537092053.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut